     I believe you will find the Blue Chip chronicle of=20
developments in the Buffalo newspaper situation particularly=20
interesting.  There are now only 14 cities in the United States=20
with a daily newspaper whose weekday circulation exceeds that of=20
the Buffalo News.  But the real story has been the growth in=20
Sunday circulation.  Six years ago, prior to introduction of a=20
Sunday edition of the News, the long-established Courier-Express,=20
as the only Sunday newspaper published in Buffalo, had=20
circulation of 272,000.  The News now has Sunday circulation of=20
367,000, a 35% gain - even though the number of households within=20
the primary circulation area has shown little change during the=20
six years.  We know of no city in the United States with a long=20
history of seven-day newspaper publication in which the=20
percentage of households purchasing the Sunday newspaper has=20
grown at anything like this rate.  To the contrary, in most=20
cities household penetration figures have grown negligibly, or=20
not at all.  Our key managers in Buffalo - Henry Urban, Stan=20
Lipsey, Murray Light, Clyde Pinson, Dave Perona and Dick Feather=20
- deserve great credit for this unmatched expansion in Sunday=20
readership.

